      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Looking at this again, I realize that I somehow managed to duplicate IsSubclassOf instead of writing the function that I actually meant, the second mention of IsSubclassOf was supposed to be requesting Type.IsAssignableFrom().\nAnother useful function for dealing with arrays of objects and such would be Type.GetElementType()",
